  "closes": "Establishes, by independent non-runtime re-derivation with G0 byte-exact parity against the shipped Rust hash anchors, that amphora-run-provenance's verify_run is an internal-consistency predicate (15/15 non-recomputing mutations fail closed) and NOT a tamper-evidence predicate (0/8 consistent re-forges detected); identifies root_hash as the unique minimally sufficient 32-byte external anchor (8/8, versus at most 6/8 for any single component hash); separates anchor COMPLETENESS from anchor LOCALIZATION (root-only localizes 0/8, four component hashes localize 8/8); and shows constructively that a DSSE Ed25519 attestation over {run_id, root_hash} restores 8/8 detection in-band under cold key custody but 0/8 under hot-key custody on the producing host -- converting the module's open 'Phase-1 controlled-key signing pipeline' item from a checkbox into a testable key-custody requirement with a measured threat model.",
