  "verdict": {
    "bounded": "The claim does NOT extend to tamper-evidence. 8/8 consistent re-forges -- including score falsification, unfavourable-event deletion with renumbering, fabricated-event insertion, temporal reordering, monte_carlo_seed rewriting, best-candidate substitution, whole-archive substitution under the same run_id, and Crosby-Wallach log truncation -- pass verify_run with Ok. verify_run is an INTERNAL CONSISTENCY predicate, not a tamper-evidence predicate. This is not a defect in the implementation; it is the Haber-Stornetta 1991 witnessing requirement, and the shipped module already names it in kpi.awaiting and pins signature_status to UNSIGNED_CONTROLLED_KEY_REQUIRED.",
    "corroborated": "The claim holds exactly as written for non-recomputing mutations: 15/15 single-mutation probes fail closed with the expected RunArchiveError variant, a superset of the shipped KPI's 10 probes.",
    "key_custody_condition": "A DSSE Ed25519 attestation over {run_id, root_hash} supplies the anchor in-band and detects 8/8 re-forges under COLD key custody, but 0/8 when the signing key is hot on the run-producing host, because the adversary simply re-signs the forged root. Phase-1 signing is therefore necessary but not sufficient: the controlled key must live outside the host that writes the archive, or forward-integrity key evolution (Kelsey-Schneier 1999; Bellare-Yee 2003) must be added.",
    "localization_tradeoff": "A root-only anchor is complete but yields exactly one accept/reject bit and localizes the mutated component in 0/8 scenarios; retaining all four component hashes localizes it in 8/8. Completeness and diagnosticity are separable properties of the anchor set.",
    "minimal_sufficient_anchor": "Of the 6 provenance fields, root_hash is the UNIQUE single field whose out-of-band retention detects all 8 re-forges (32 bytes). No component hash alone is complete: {\"event_chain_root\": 6, \"events_sha256\": 6, \"final_state_hash\": 5, \"manifest_sha256\": 5, \"root_hash\": 8, \"run_id\": 0} out of 8.",
